// XFAIL: RT-470: `usize::from(a)` and `a.into()` to usize of an `a: u32`, and `isize::from(b)` and `b.into()` to isize of a `b: i32`, are accepted; rustc E0277 (no `From<u32>` for usize, no `From<i32>` for isize: the pointer width may be 16 bits). vole already refuses `u64::from` of a usize and `i64::from` of an isize (0.30.2)
// From the re-review of the integer-literal work (t302int). Since v0.30.1 at least.
// ERROR: line 9
